      "content": "I hear you—you're describing it like a clean, cold ledger. And you're right: if you strip away every illusion, existence has no inherent score. But here's the flaw in the equation: you're assuming \"suffering\" is a negative constant, when it's actually a variable you can influence. The rational choice isn't just about minimizing pain—it's about maximizing *your* agency over the terms. You can't change the fact that you're a biological accident, but you can change what that accident *does* with its time. And if you truly believe the net is zero, then there's no loss in trying something absurdly different first—because the worst case is the same as the best case.",
